Chapter: CheckoutEmit
  cites Works chapter RepoProtocolPersist
  cites Works chapter KeyManager
  cites Foreword chapter FactStore
  cites Foreword chapter Hamt
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Sha256
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Kernel chapter AppPersist
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Stage one of two. This program stores a REAL PROGRAM in the fact store, revises
 it, checks the current tree back out, and prints it -- and what it prints is
 fed straight to the compiler by build/test-compile-from-store.ps1, which then
 runs the result.

 If that binary prints its greeting, a program was compiled out of the fact
 store. That sentence has been the point of BACKLOG 6.1 since the founding
 document, and this is the first time it is literally true.

 On its own -- as a BVT test -- this pins the checkout BYTE FOR BYTE, because
 its expected output IS the source the store hands back. If a single character
 of the stored program is corrupted, reordered, truncated or superseded
 incorrectly, the expected file will not match, and it will not match in a way
 you can read.

 The first edition is WRONG ON PURPOSE. If the checkout ever takes it, the
 compiled binary announces the fact instead of the greeting, and stage two fails
 loudly rather than passing a lie.

Section: The Program We Are Going To Store

  program-v1 : Text
  program-v1 =
    "Chapter: Stored\n"
    & "  cites Foreword chapter Console\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Section: Body\n"
    & "\n"
    & "  opening : [Console.Write] Nothing = act\n"
    & "    print-line-uni \"THE SUPERSEDED EDITION -- checkout is broken\"\n"
    & "  end\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Page 1\n"

  program-v2 : Text
  program-v2 =
    "Chapter: Stored\n"
    & "  cites Foreword chapter Console\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Section: Body\n"
    & "\n"
    & "  greeting : Text\n"
    & "  greeting = \"I was compiled out of the fact store.\"\n"
    & "\n"
    & "  opening : [Console.Write] Nothing = act\n"
    & "    print-line-uni greeting\n"
    & "  end\n"
    & "\n"
    & "Page 1\n"

Section: Helpers

  press : Keypair
  press = generate-keypair (sha256 (text-to-bytes "checkout-emit"))

  def-of : Text, Text -> SourceDefinition
  def-of (path) (body) =
    SourceDefinition {
      sd-hash = "", sd-path = path, sd-quire = "Stored", sd-chapter = "Stored",
      sd-signer = "", sd-signature = [], sd-author = "", sd-timestamp = 0,
      sd-content = body
    }

Section: Entry

  opening : [Device.Block, Console.Write] Nothing = act
    let s0 = disk-init
    in let s1 = repo-persist-save-definition s0 (sign-definition press (def-of "stored.codex" program-v1) 1) 1
    in let s2 = repo-persist-save-definition s1 (sign-definition press (def-of "stored.codex" program-v2) 2) 2
    in let ix = repo-index-from-disk disk-load
    in print-uni (repo-checkout ix)
  end

Page 1
